<section id="About">
    <div class="title">
         <h1>Our Story — Flour, Water, and Passion</h1>
    </div>
    <p> Founded in 2018, The Golden Whisk started as a small weekend passion project in a home kitchen. Head baker Evelyn Vance wanted to recreate the comforting, slow-fermented European breads she enjoyed during her travels. What began as a couple of loaves shared with neighbors quickly grew into a bustling storefront loved by the local community.</p>
<h3>Our Core Values</h3>
<ul>
    <li>
        Quality First: We source organic flour, seasonal fruits, and real dairy from nearby farms.</li>
        <li>Time-Honoured Tradition: We never rush our dough. Good bread takes patience, time, and careful hands.</li>
        <li>Community Core: We donate our unsold bread at the end of every day to local shelters.
    </li>
</ul>
